 `item({path, delta})` in `Servex/agents/page_tools.js`: `page_set` generalised to any Item class. `delta` is one log line, the object `Item.set()` takes. A key naming a method calls it, a key naming a child walks into it, anything else assigns (`set_one` in `core/Item/Item.js`; there is no second apply).
 
-**The three verbs** (merge 1 of the plan at [/live/plan/item-tool/](/live/plan/item-tool/)): `get`, `set` and `call` sit beside `delta` and `read`. Each becomes exactly the `delta`/`read` a caller would have written — `verbs_to_delta()` at the top of `run_item_now` — so everything below is unchanged: `item({path, get:"a.b"})` = `read:"a.b"`; `item({path, set:{title:"x"}})` = `delta:{title:"x"}`; `item({path, call:"tasks.add", args:{title:"x"}})` = `delta:{tasks:{add:{title:"x"}}}`; `item({path, call:"start"})` = `delta:{start:{}}`. A `set` key that names a method or a list, or a `call` whose last step isn't a method (or is a query), is refused by name, checked against `surface_of(Class)` and `node.lists()` — the same data `instructions.methods` comes from. More than one of `delta`/`read`/`get`/`set`/`call` in one call is refused. Full detail and the AI-facing version: [core/Page/doc/ai-api.md](/framework/core/Page/doc/ai-api.md), "The three verbs". Test: `node Servex/agents/item-verbs.test.mjs`.
+**The three verbs** (merge 1 of the plan at [/live/plan/item-tool/](/live/plan/item-tool/)): `get`, `set` and `call` sit beside `delta` and `read`. Each becomes exactly the `delta`/`read` a caller would have written — `verbs_to_delta()` at the top of `run_item_now` — so everything below is unchanged: `item({path, get:"a.b"})` = `read:"a.b"`; `item({path, set:{title:"x"}})` = `delta:{title:"x"}`; `item({path, call:"tasks.add", args:{title:"x"}})` = `delta:{tasks:{add:{title:"x"}}}`; `item({path, call:"start"})` = `delta:{start:{}}`. A `set` key that names a method or a list, or a `call` whose last step isn't a method (or is a query), is refused by name, checked against `surface_of(Class)` and `node.lists()` — the same data `instructions.methods` comes from. More than one of `delta`/`read`/`get`/`set`/`call` in one call is refused. `args` sent as JSON text (a client whose schema shows it as a string) is parsed first (`parse_args`); any other string stays a string. Full detail and the AI-facing version: [core/Page/doc/ai-api.md](/framework/core/Page/doc/ai-api.md), "The three verbs". Test: `node Servex/agents/item-verbs.test.mjs`.
 
 - **Which log:** a url's folder holds `task.jsonl` (Task), else `session.jsonl` (Session, `core/Session/Session.js`), else `page.jsonl` (Page). `task.jsonl` beside a `page.jsonl` means a task folder. A `class` key on line 1 wins when `Item.types` registers that name (`class_for`); an unknown name falls back to the file's own class.
 - **`path` is a site-absolute URL, never a repo-relative one with `public/` on the front** (seen 2026-11-07, item-validate): `item({path: "/framework/ai/sessions/…/", delta})`, not `item({path: "public/framework/ai/sessions/…/", delta})`. A `path` that starts with `public/` resolves against `PUBLIC` the same way a correct one does, so it lands at `public/public/…` instead — a folder git already ignores (`.gitignore:256`, `public/public/`), so the call still answers `{ok:true, line:{…}, size:{…}}` and LOOKS like it landed, but the real `session.jsonl` (or `page.jsonl`) a reviewer or a fresh agent reads never gets the line. Found when a minion's own "log" calls through `mcp__local__item` left no trace in its task's `session.jsonl`; `public/public/` held the misdirected writes instead (removed, nothing of value was in it). The safe route when unsure: `node .claude/hooks/append.mjs <absolute-path-to-task.jsonl-or-session.jsonl> <lines.json>`, which takes a real filesystem path, never a URL.
